  "canon:title": "Angioedema due to ACE inhibitors: common and inadequately diagnosed.",
  "canon:abstract": "The estimated incidence of angioedema during angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor treatment is between 1 and 7 per thousand patients. This potentially serious adverse effect is often preceded by minor manifestations that may serve as a warning.",
  "canon:text": "Angioedema due to ACE inhibitors: common and inadequately diagnosed. The estimated incidence of angioedema during angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor treatment is between 1 and 7 per thousand patients. This potentially serious adverse effect is often preceded by minor manifestations that may serve as a warning.",
